They met in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men."
They will kill him. And on the third day, he will rise from the dead." When the disciples heard this, they went into hiding, their hearts filled with deep sorrow. Jesus pays the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, a tax collector came to Peter. And they asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
Yes, he does, he answered. When Peter entered the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "Who among earth's rulers collects taxes and fees? Do they collect them from their own children or from others?"
"From others," Peter answered. "Then children ought not to pay," Jesus said to him.
But we do not want to anger them. So go to the lake and cast your fishing line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You will find there the exact coin you need. Take it and give it to them for each of our taxes.
